## Pipeline

Every push and pull request runs the `CI` workflow. It needs no AWS account.

| Job | What it checks |
| --- | -------------- |
| Lambda function | Unit tests of the function; builds `build/lambda.zip` |
{%- if authType == 'jwt' %}
| Token authorizer | Unit tests of `authorizer/` |
{%- endif %}
| Terraform | `terraform fmt -check`, `terraform validate`, `terraform test` (a plan of `infra/terraform.tfvars.json` against mocked providers), TFLint |
| Security scan | Trivy scan of `infra/`; fails on high and critical findings |
| Documentation | `mkdocs build --strict` of `docs/` |
{%- if values.enableCICD %}

The `Deploy` workflow plans on pull requests and applies on `main` once an AWS
role and a state bucket are configured. Until then it reports that and skips
both steps.
{%- endif %}
